# Material interno de marca — no se publica
Branding/

# Versiones de trabajo del sitio
web/

# Sistema
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Archives. An archive is the most likely shape of internal material — "send me the logos" produces
# a zip — and nothing can read inside one from here, so the extension is the whole signal. A file
# that is MEANT to be downloadable goes in downloads/, which is not ignored: putting it there is how
# the decision to publish it gets written down. Added with handbook v4.0.0, which added the same
# extensions to the gate's tracked-material scan.
*.zip
*.rar
*.7z
*.tar
*.tgz
*.gz
!downloads/**

# Lighthouse run output. The repository is the web root, so a committed report is a PUBLISHED
# report — with the site's full audit trail and every URL it walked. The gate reads it from the
# runner's working directory and never needs it committed; `.gate-measures.json` is the part that
# is meant to be kept, and that one is tracked.
.lighthouseci/
